+## 5. The universal quantifier and the kill
+
+The logical claim needed for a row kill is exactly
+
+```text
+For every polynomial pair realizing the necessary R063 parent data, every
+Prop-6.3 child partition compatible with that pair has nonintegral I'_M.
+```
+
+It is not enough to compute one representative or one truncated child. For
+R063 the claim follows from the preceding finite exhaustion:
+
+1. Assume a polynomial pair realizes R063. Proposition 6.4 licenses the
+   Proposition 6.3 descent, which produces the polynomial, \(Y\)-monic child
+   pair of §1.
+2. The zero/nonzero first-support alternatives are exhaustive and leave the
+   singleton own vector \((3,7)\); there is no set-valued child label.
+3. Proposition 4.6 and the actual orbit size force the sole level patterns in
