+## 4. The unique printed fixed-list child pattern
+
+At \(D'_3\), Proposition 4.6 gives
+
+\[
+ P_3=V'_4d'_3/d'_4=7,qquad
+ Q_3=P_3(n'-M'_3)/d'_3=2.
+\]
+
+The entering stabilizer is 1 and \(\delta'_3=-2\), so the orbit increment is
+1. Containing selected multiplicity 7 forces the single factor
+\(p'_3=(\pi-c)^7\), unique up to translation. It is above the average
+\(7/2\) and continues to \(D'_2\).
+
+At \(D'_2\),
+
+\[
+ P_2=V'_3d'_2/d'_3=14,qquad Q_2=7,qquad
+ A_2=\operatorname{den}(-1/3)=3.
+\]
+
+Write the Galois-compatible factor shape as
+
+\[
+ p'_2=\pi^z\prod_j(\pi^3-c_j)^{r_j}.
+\]
+
+It must satisfy \(z+3\sum r_j=14\), have at most seven distinct roots, and
+contain multiplicity \(V'_2=3\). A multiplicity equal to
+\(P_2/Q_2=2\) is forbidden by the Proposition 4.6 differential equation:
+at such a root the leading terms cancel while its nonzero right side still has
+the original order. The possible zero exponents are
+\(z=2,5,8,11,14\). The first is excluded by that equality; the last three
+cannot contain a multiplicity 3 orbit. Therefore the sole pattern is
+
+\[
+ \boxed{p'_2=\pi^5(\pi^3-c)^3.}
+\]
+
+Its four \(P'\)-root packets have reduced multiplicities \(5,3,3,3\).
+Since \(m'/d'_2=2\), their actual \(P'\)-root counts are
+
+\[
+ 10,6,6,6,\qquad 10+3\cdot6=28=m'.
+\]
+
+Similarly \(n'/d'_2=3\) gives \(Q'\)-root counts
+\(15,9,9,9\), totaling 42. This double degree exhaustion is the key response
+to the proposed incomplete-partition failure: an extra disjoint packet would
+exceed a polynomial degree. The same counts are obtained by the frozen
+`inverse_top` conservation identity (lines 70–97) from the parent's unique
+actual-\(L\) pattern \(\pi^{12}(\pi^{10}-c)^3\).
+
+Every reduced multiplicity is strictly above the major threshold 2. Hence
+there is **no child minor packet** at this split and no minor family available
+for later re-expansion. Proposition 5.3 sends each factor through the same
+fixed characteristic list from \(D'_2\) directly to \(D'_1\). At \(r=1\),
+the unchanged Proposition 4.6 constant differential equation makes the
+leading \(P'\)-polynomial squarefree and disjoint from the leading
+\(Q'\)-polynomial; these \(D'_1\) discs are final. Inserting an extra free
+\(W\)-level is not licensed by the printed closure.
+
+For a reduced multiplicity \(r\), put \(\rho=2r\). At \(D'_2\) the packet
+intercept gives
+
+\[
+ \kappa(r)={14(r-2)\over3},\qquad
+ \delta_{\rm fin}=2-{70\kappa\over70\rho-28},qquad
+ J_{\rm packet}={42\rho\kappa\over70\rho-28}.
+\]
+
+Thus the three nonzero \(r=3\) packets have
+\(\rho_P=6,\rho_Q=9,\delta=7/6\) and contribute 3 each. The zero
+\(r=5\) packet has
+\(\rho_P=10,\rho_Q=15,\delta=13/24\) and contributes \(35/4\). The shifted
+Theorem 5.1 sum forced under existence is therefore
+
+\[
+ I'_M=3\cdot3+{35\over4}=\boxed{{71\over4}},qquad I'_m=2.
+\]
+
+The actual stabilizers provide an independent check. A nonzero coefficient at
+\(\delta'_2=-1/3\) gives \(L'=3\), hence
+\(A=\operatorname{den}(3\cdot7/6)=2\); residues
+\((\rho_P,\rho_Q)=(6,9)\equiv(0,1)\pmod2\) pass. The zero factor adds no
+denominator, so its actual \(L'=1\), not 3. Its final increment is
+
+\[
+ A=\operatorname{den}(1\cdot13/24)=24,
+\]
+
+and \((10,15)\) satisfies neither allowed \(0/1\) residue. Thus there are zero
+Galois-valid complete child configurations. The frozen producer's \(A=8\)
+used the nonzero lane's denominator on the zero lane. Its values
+\(33/2,103/6\), and the six-value depth sweep arise only after inserting
+unlicensed levels below \(D'_2\); they are not outcomes of Moh's printed
+fixed-list closure. The sealed replay independently returns “one selected
+pattern, zero complete, ungated \(71/4\), zero-lane \(L'=1,A=24\).”
+
+## 5. The universal quantifier and the kill
+
+The logical claim needed for a row kill is exactly
+
+```text
+For every polynomial pair realizing the necessary R063 parent data, every
+Prop-6.3 child partition compatible with that pair has nonintegral I'_M.
+```
+
+It is not enough to compute one representative or one truncated child. For
+R063 the claim follows from the preceding finite exhaustion:
+
+1. Assume a polynomial pair realizes R063. Proposition 6.4 licenses the
+   Proposition 6.3 descent, which produces the polynomial, \(Y\)-monic child
+   pair of §1.
+2. The zero/nonzero first-support alternatives are exhaustive and leave the
+   singleton own vector \((3,7)\); there is no set-valued child label.
+3. Proposition 4.6 and the actual orbit size force the sole level patterns in
+   §4. Their packet counts exhaust all 28 roots of \(P'\) and all 42 roots of
+   \(Q'\). Coefficients remain undetermined, but cannot change these counts,
+   radii, or contributions.
+4. All four packets are above-average major packets. Shifted Proposition 5.3
+   takes them directly to final \(D'_1\). Therefore no omitted minor
+   re-expansion and no extra major split can alter the complete sum.
+5. The monic resultant degree must then equal \(71/4\), contradicting §1.
+   Equivalently, because the child is minor-free, shifted Theorem 4.7(iii)
+   would require \(71/4=2+k\) with integral \(k\ge0\), also impossible.
+
+The argument never promotes a representative to a pair. It assumes a realizing
+pair only to derive a child that every such realization must have, and then
+contradicts an exact polynomial invariant. This is precisely the legitimate
+use of a necessary configuration.
+
+Accordingly **R063 is DEAD** and may be promoted: the frozen residual 65 becomes
+**64**. The six rows rejected by the earlier exact-contact gate are not revived
+as kills here, so there is no 59-to-58 arithmetic.
+
+The child Xu condition is genuinely descent-sensitive. On the 46 licensed
+\(u_s=1\) rows in the frozen census, the child has no surviving Xu-compatible
+configuration on R001, R025–R028, R057, R058, and R063; the first seven were
+already excluded at the parent, while R063 is the new row-level consequence.
+The shifted minor inequality also removes integral child alternatives on R001,
+R002, and R013, though R002 and R013 retain other alternatives and are not row
+kills. R009 and R050 survive with child \(I'_M=8\). The twenty \(u_s>1\)
+rows are untouched because their child radius/top identification is not
+licensed by these inputs.
+
+## 6. FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+* **Flag/place/series:** the parent source tower, its principal minor family,
