+## 5. The universal quantifier and the kill
+
+The logical claim needed for a row kill is exactly
+
+```text
+For every polynomial pair realizing the necessary R063 parent data, every
+Prop-6.3 child partition compatible with that pair has nonintegral I'_M.
+```
+
+It is not enough to compute one representative or one truncated child. For
+R063 the claim follows from the preceding finite exhaustion:
+
+1. Assume a polynomial pair realizes R063. Proposition 6.4 licenses the
+   Proposition 6.3 descent, which produces the polynomial, \(Y\)-monic child
+   pair of §1.
+2. The zero/nonzero first-support alternatives are exhaustive and leave the
+   singleton own vector \((3,7)\); there is no set-valued child label.
+3. Proposition 4.6 and the actual orbit size force the sole level patterns in
+   §4. Their packet counts exhaust all 28 roots of \(P'\) and all 42 roots of
+   \(Q'\). Coefficients remain undetermined, but cannot change these counts,
+   radii, or contributions.
+4. All four packets are above-average major packets. Shifted Proposition 5.3
+   takes them directly to final \(D'_1\). Therefore no omitted minor
+   re-expansion and no extra major split can alter the complete sum.
+5. The monic resultant degree must then equal \(71/4\), contradicting §1.
+   Equivalently, because the child is minor-free, shifted Theorem 4.7(iii)
+   would require \(71/4=2+k\) with integral \(k\ge0\), also impossible.
+
+The argument never promotes a representative to a pair. It assumes a realizing
+pair only to derive a child that every such realization must have, and then
+contradicts an exact polynomial invariant. This is precisely the legitimate
+use of a necessary configuration.
+
+Accordingly **R063 is DEAD** and may be promoted: the frozen residual 65 becomes
+**64**. The six rows rejected by the earlier exact-contact gate are not revived
+as kills here, so there is no 59-to-58 arithmetic.
